Session corrections — 24 July 2026 — Institutional path migration (Fase 2, Despliegue B) — VP-SEC-009 to 015
The institutional (university/workplace email) adhesion path, flagged in the 23 July audit as bypassing the participation_token system entirely (routes/institucional.js performing its own direct adhesions insert), was migrated onto the same AdhesionService built the same day, closing seven further findings identified during the auditor’s design review of this migration: OTP stored in plaintext (VP-SEC-009, fixed — only an HMAC of the code is now stored, never the code itself); OTP valid 24 hours (VP-SEC-010, reduced to 10 minutes); Math.random() for OTP generation (VP-SEC-011, replaced with crypto.randomInt()); no reCAPTCHA on send-otp (VP-SEC-012, added); rate limiting insufficient and racy (VP-SEC-013, replaced with an atomic, multi-dimensional check — email+protest, IP, institutional domain, a global ceiling — counting real rows rather than maintaining a separate mutable counter); no attempt counter on OTP verification (VP-SEC-014, added, transactional, capped at five attempts); OTP consumption and adhesion creation not atomic (VP-SEC-015, resolved via a new RPC, verify_institutional_otp_and_create_adhesion, which locks and consumes the OTP and calls create_verified_adhesion() internally in the same transaction — a failed adhesion now rolls back the OTP consumption too).
email_hash is no longer returned to the client in the verify-otp response.
A related front-end finding, unconnected to the audit but found while touching this same screen: VerifyInstitucionalScreen.vue’s generarHashFalso() fabricated a plausible-looking sha256:-prefixed string as the displayed “receipt” whenever the backend’s real receipt was absent, meaning a person could see what looked like cryptographic confirmation for an adhesion that may never have been created. Removed; the screen now shows an honest error if a receipt is genuinely missing, since the new atomic path guarantees one is present on any real success.
